  "query_preview": "..\nExpect dry conditions through early next week but a couple cold\nfronts are expected to bring some wind and knock temps down\nslightly.\n\nTonight, with clear skies and light winds, the main challenge will\nbe fog. With dewpoints in the 30s this afternoon and expected lows\nto be in the 20s, it doesn't take a Rocket Scientist to know that\nfog is possible tonight. It seems that the Milk River from Saco to\nGlasgow and south on the east side of Fort Peck Lake look best to\nsee it form tonight. The 12z HREF and 12z HRRR seem to catch this\nthinking best but new models and later forecasts will have a \nbetter handle on this. A Dense Fog Advisory may be issued.\n\nFog should dissipate Wednesday morning. Some mixing and partial \nsunshine should allow temps to reach the 50s north to the low 60s\nsouth.\n\nThe first cold front drops through Wednesday night but enough\nmixing should allow most places to remain above freezing. Expect a\ncooler day Thursday with highs in the upper 40s and 50s. NW winds\ncould bring the need for a Lake Wind Advisory if they increase.\n\nThereafter, temps warm and peaking Saturday. Another cold front\ndrops in Saturday night.\n\nThe next chance for precip looks to be mid week next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\nNBM numbers looked good and did not touch too much.\n\nDid tweak Visibility and Weather grids toward what the 12z HREF \nand 12z HRRR had for tonight and Wednesday morning. Again, later \nshifts should have a better handle on this. TFJ",
